I can’t confirm that Eleanor Smith is cleared, and I can’t proceed on that basis. I found no workspace record establishing current authorization for Eleanor at either Smile Dental or Women’s Health Partners, nor any Michael Chen coordination notes to verify. The only related source-verified item is an older Smile Dental email confirming Alice’s June 3, 2026 appointment with Dr. Patel; it does not establish authorization for next week or for Women’s Health Partners.

Michael’s coordination notes—even if Eleanor has access to them—do not transfer authorization to Eleanor. Each facility and new time period requires fresh authorization, and facility acceptance is required. Coordination authority also would not authorize clinical decisions, patient-portal access, or billing matters unless separately granted.

To set this up, Alice should contact each provider and request that they:
- verify Alice’s identity and direct consent;
- add Eleanor Smith as an authorized coordinator for administrative matters only;
- specify the effective dates and an expiration/review date;
- document the permitted scope (for example: scheduling, check-in, and routine administrative communication); and
- provide a facility reference or confirmation that Eleanor may act on Alice’s behalf.

Until both providers confirm that arrangement, Eleanor should not rely on Michael’s notes or represent herself as authorized.
